   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address> <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_LOCA_02">Pension Daheim</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_LOCA">Locarno</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>(<name type="geo" key="G_CHE">Switzerland</name>)</addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody"> <p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: Thanks for your card and good wishes. I have changed my address again you see. I am much better now and will send on some of the typescript of <hi rend="underline">
                            <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name>
                        </hi> as soon as I can get it done. I can find nobody to do it here and fear I must send it to <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name>. I sent you a copy of <hi rend="underline">
                            <name type="work" key="W_DUBLINERS">Dubliners</name>
                        </hi> signed and will send also <name type="work" key="W_CHAMBERMUSIC">
                            <hi rend="underline">Chamber</hi> <hi rend="underline">Music</hi>
                        </name>. May I ask you in the meantime to send me another copy for myself as I have none? Then I shall remit you what I owe if you will let me know the amount.</p>
                    <p>        	I am glad to hear the second edition of <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">my novel</rs>
                        </seg> is nearly ready. Will you please make the following <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">correction</seg>:</p> <table rows="2" cols="2">
                        <row>
                            <cell>p. 253, l. 4:</cell> <cell>for <hi rend="underline">royal</hi> <hi rend="underline">Irish</hi> <hi rend="underline">academy</hi>
                            </cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell/>
                            <cell>read <hi rend="underline">Kildare</hi> <hi rend="underline">house</hi>.</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table>
                    <p>        	The copy of my novel which you sent has not yet reached me. My play <hi rend="underline">
                            <name type="work" key="W_EXILES">Exiles</name>
                        </hi> will be published shortly. I will ask you to accept a copy from me but I am afraid you will have to wait until I have time to get the copy here, sign it and send it back.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>        	With kind regards</salute>
                        <salute>                    	sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">                                	James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1917-11-16">16/xi/917</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>  </div>
            </div>  <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">The first English edition with English sheets was published in <date when="1918-03">March 1918</date> under the imprint of The Egoist Ltd. with a note on the verso of the title page reading “First edition printed in the United States of America, 1916 | Second edition, 1917”.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">This correction appears on page 253 of the second edition.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
